{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548868-dr-john-dee-the-queens-conjuror","id":1548868,"title":"Dr John Dee the queens conjuror","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-02T01:09:43-08:00","id":1548868,"title":"Dr John Dee the queens conjuror","content":"Reading this book at the moment and it's great. He must have been an inspiration for the Tremere. He might have actually coined the word 'thaumaturgy' and his view was magic was just another form of science. Worked with royalty and nobility by providing advice generated from a mixture of science and magic and spent a large part of fortune hunting down books containing scientific and occult knowledge. Definitely recommended reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T01:43:01-08:00","id":1548869,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that Dee is a Tremere in one of the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T01:57:27-08:00","id":1548870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548868-dr-john-dee-the-queens-conjuror?p=1548869#post1548869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn that Dee is a Tremere in one of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't suprised me. I've understood it to be that all manner of historical people show up as vampires in 1ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T02:03:49-08:00","id":1548871,"title":"","content":"You are not wrong<br /> He was a mage of the Order of Hermes who was Embraced into the Tremere clan of vampires in 1607 CE and was both in the 1st edition Clanbook: Tremere and in Encyclopaedia Vampirica (tho the later is a bit full of inconsitstencies and quessings, since it was written by numerous popular vampires and more of an IC cosurce than a &quot;real&quot; one )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T02:23:28-08:00","id":1548872,"title":"","content":"Having a flick through his Wikipedia page, there are two sources (admittedly both are over 100 years old) that mention Dee's death isn't listed in his parish register, and there's no gravestone...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T12:11:40-08:00","id":1548883,"title":"","content":"I always thought of Dee has a sort of ex-Arcanium and a hedge-magician.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T12:43:58-08:00","id":1548885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548868-dr-john-dee-the-queens-conjuror?p=1548871#post1548871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not wrong<br /> He was a mage of the Order of Hermes who was Embraced into the Tremere clan of vampires in 1607 CE and was both in the 1st edition Clanbook: Tremere and in Encyclopaedia Vampirica (tho the later is a bit full of inconsitstencies and quessings, since it was written by numerous popular vampires and more of an IC cosurce than a &quot;real&quot; one )</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, John Dee is not in the 1e Clanbook Tremere (at least not a full character writeup; he might be mentioned). John Dee is in the very first World of Darkness sourcebook with full stats. I think by the time of 1e Clanbook Tremere they were already regretting including such a famous person as Dee as a vampire. The Comte de Saint-Germain, another famous occultist from the 18th century, is included in the 1e Clanbook Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 03-04-2025, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T12:46:35-08:00","id":1548886,"title":"","content":"Saint-Germain is much less of a historical figure than Dee was (even his existence is doubted by some scholars), so he would make a much better candidate to be Embraced as a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T13:05:45-08:00","id":1548888,"title":"","content":"I actually remember John Dee being a sorcerer back in 2e's Sorcerer. Honestly, him being a hedge magician makes more sense in terms of history and his abilities. I kind of get the feeling that his vampire status in 1e was partially a product of Masquerade being the only line available back then. It reminded me of how Crowley was made a vampire back in one of the Masquerade books, even though in terms of occupation he definitely seems more like a sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T13:13:41-08:00","id":1548889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548868-dr-john-dee-the-queens-conjuror?p=1548888#post1548888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, him being a hedge magician makes more sense in terms of history and his abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's kinda implied that he maybe was. <i>Vampirica</i> gives his embrace as being 1607, that's like a year or two before his death. So, all the stuff he's known for, was stuff he did pre-embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T08:42:38-08:00","id":1548906,"title":"","content":"In all honesty one could more easily imagine Doctor Dee\u2019s sometime accomplice Edward Kelly as a vampire - given the latter seems to have been the one who settled conveniently close to the Tremere base of operations in Central Europe (At least for a time) and generally appears to have been a more shady customer.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, given John Dee seems to have suffered a steep decline in fortunes prior to his death, it\u2019s easier to imagine him considering vampirism as a viable alternative to the afterlife than - for instance - Charlemagne.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do feel that as a rule of thumb historical figures who \u2018went out at the top\u2019 should not be be seriously considered for vampirism - especially when they\u2019re persons who, by definition, have been told all their lives that they are God\u2019s special favourite (and can reasonably expect to die surrounded by a legion of mourners).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T15:09:43-08:00","id":1548927,"title":"","content":"It's been quite some time since I read The Fall of London, but didn't that have an occultist Malkavian who has sometimes masqueraded as John Dee since the latter's death? Easy enough to retcon that figure into whoever people were really dealing with when they <i>thought</i> it was an embraced John Dee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T16:45:34-08:00","id":1548930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548868-dr-john-dee-the-queens-conjuror?p=1548927#post1548927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been quite some time since I read The Fall of London, but didn't that have an occultist Malkavian who has sometimes masqueraded as John Dee since the latter's death? Easy enough to retcon that figure into whoever people were really dealing with when they <i>thought</i> it was an embraced John Dee.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that, but I think it was London by Night for Victorian Age Vampire, not Fall of London.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T16:47:03-08:00","id":1548931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548868-dr-john-dee-the-queens-conjuror?p=1548906#post1548906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In all honesty one could more easily imagine Doctor Dee\u2019s sometime accomplice Edward Kelly as a vampire - given the latter seems to have been the one who settled conveniently close to the Tremere base of operations in Central Europe (At least for a time) and generally appears to have been a more shady customer.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, given John Dee seems to have suffered a steep decline in fortunes prior to his death, it\u2019s easier to imagine him considering vampirism as a viable alternative to the afterlife than - for instance - Charlemagne.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do feel that as a rule of thumb historical figures who \u2018went out at the top\u2019 should not be be seriously considered for vampirism - especially when they\u2019re persons who, by definition, have been told all their lives that they are God\u2019s special favourite (and can reasonably expect to die surrounded by a legion of mourners).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Kelley, I think that one could pin him as a psychic, given how Dee specifically chose the man to be his seer, although tying him to the Tremere later in life is clever and sort of fits with some of the alchemical exploits he got up to after he and Dee parted ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T03:49:10-08:00","id":1548942,"title":"","content":"Also, if any vampire on Earth were not only willing but well-able to pass himself off as Vampire John Dee it would benefit Vampire Edward Kelly! (I believe that, even in life, Mr Kelly was not above exploiting Doctor Dee\u2019s credulity - which would certainly explain the somewhat tense nature of their partnership).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T17:53:12-08:00","id":1548973,"title":"","content":"Kelly's assertation that the angels he was in communion with wanted them to wife swap probably didn't help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T12:43:06-08:00","id":1548987,"title":"","content":"Not all magic is Sex Magic, but clearly at least a few magicians feel that it <i>should</i> be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}